Thinking about design principles:
Trying to solve a design problem takes experience. There is also no such thing as a simple answer / one thing for all type of solution. 

One thing to keep in mind: Dont try to solve every problem from first principles. Experience teaches to solve problems using idea previously already used. Most patterns solve a specific design problem, making OOP flexible elegant and reusable.
This also helps old designers identify and immediately reuse the design pattern.


The MVC pattern:
Model. /View / Controller triad of classes.:
Model -> application object
View -> Screen presentation and
Controller -> The way User interact with it.


A view must ensrue that its appearance reflects the state of the model. 

#image("assets/image.png")

The model-view relationship shows the Observer pattern, while view-controller shows a Strategy pattern. 

These design patterns are discussed later in the book.

